-map-links{row-gap:0!important}.c3-map-links a{padding:.55rem 0}ul[role=list][style*="minmax(13rem,1fr)"]{grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(min(13rem,100%),1fr))!important}</style><style>.c3-aerial .c3ph-hero,.c3-aerial-close .c3ph-hero{max-width:760px}</style><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A condo is cheaper to buy and easier to rent by the night. A house has grown more in value and is easier to finance. Find the row that fits you:</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>Condo or house: which suits each kind of investor</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">If this is you</th><th scope="col">The better choice</th><th scope="col">Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">You want the lowest price into a beach rental</th><td data-label="The better choice">A condo</td><td data-label="Why">Oceanfront: about half under $200,000</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">You are counting on the price to rise</th><td data-label="The better choice">A house</td><td data-label="Why">Houses fell less after 2006</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">You want short-term rentals near the ocean</th><td data-label="The better choice">An oceanfront condo</td><td data-label="Why">94 in 100 for sale say they allow them</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">You need an FHA or VA loan</th><td data-label="The better choice">Most likely a house</td><td data-label="Why">Only 9 FHA-approved condo projects</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">You may need to sell within a few years</th><td data-label="The better choice">A house</td><td data-label="Why">12 months of condos for sale; houses 4</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">You do not want to manage a roof, a pool or the building's insurance</th><td data-label="The better choice">A condo</td><td data-label="Why">8 in 10 fees include the insurance</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The rest depends on the building: its fee, its rules and whether a lender will finance it. The <a href="#the-building" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">building section</a> below lists what we read before an offer.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="prices-over-time"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Prices over time">How have Myrtle Beach condo prices done compared with houses?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Worse than houses, and they are falling again. From its 2006 high to early 2012, the typical metro condo lost about 43 percent of its value. The typical house lost about 30 percent.</p><figure class="c3-gchart c3-cd-fig"><span class="cap" style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1.1em;line-height:1.35;margin:0 0 .5rem">Typical condo and house value, Myrtle Beach metro</span><ul class="c3-cd-legend"><li><span class="c3-cd-line" style="background:#2f6f8f"></span>Houses</li><li><span class="c3-cd-line" style="background:#c4783a"></span>Condos</li></ul><svg class="c3-cd-chart" viewBox="0 0 360 262" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Line chart of the typical home value in the Myrtle Beach metro, monthly from late 2001 to September 2026. Condos rose from about $112,000 to a high of about $197,000 in November 2006, fell to about $113,000 in January 2012, rose to about $261,000 in October 2023 and were about $231,000 in September 2026. Houses rose from about $146,000 to about $364,000, and fell less after 2007."><rect x="56" y="30" width="240" height="192" fill="rgba(255,255,255,.55)" rx="6"/><line x1="56" y1="158" x2="296" y2="158" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text class="ct" x="50" y="163" text-anchor="end">$200k</text><line x1="56" y1="94" x2="296" y2="94" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text class="ct" x="50" y="99" text-anchor="end">$300k</text><line x1="56" y1="30" x2="296" y2="30" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text class="ct" x="50" y="35" text-anchor="end">$400k</text><text class="ct" x="50" y="227" text-anchor="end">$100k</text><text class="ct" x="57.6" y="246" text-anchor="middle">2002</text><text class="ct" x="134.9" y="246" text-anchor="midd