+# data/2026-11-a/invest-condos
+
+Research data for /invest/condos/ (batch 2026-11-a). Ledger: Blog-Brain `batches/2026-11-a/invest-condos/facts.md`. Pulled 2026-11-02.
+
+| File | What | Made by |
+|---|---|---|
+| `zhvi-compare.json` | Zillow Home Value Index, Myrtle Beach metro, condo/co-op against single-family, monthly 2001-11 to 2026-09: the 2006 peak, the trough, the recovery month, changes, the condo-to-house ratio, and a December series for the chart | `python3 -I zhvi_compare.py .` |
+| `findings.json` | Every count from public records: Horry County condo units (stock, 4 percent share, owner mailing state, units per regime, by area), condo and other home sales recorded 2025-10-01 to 2026-09-30 (median, quartiles, under $200,000, by area, busiest regimes), FEMA zone at each condo sale point | `RAW=<scratch> DEEDS=<file> python3 -I analyze.py .` |
+| `listings.json` | Condos, houses and townhouses for sale in Horry County from the CRM's public map API, counted in aggregate (no address, MLS number, firm or photo): counts, medians found by halving, price and HOA fee thresholds, listing flags, the worked example's group, oceanfront buildings by mailing city. Every API URL called is in `calls`. | `python3 -I pull_listings.py .` |
+| `raw/ratio-counts.json` | Four ArcGIS count queries on county parcel layer 24: condo units and other homes, all and at the 4 percent ratio, with URLs | `python3 -I count_ratio.py .` |
+| `raw/zhvi-metro-*-mb.csv` | Header plus the Myrtle Beach, SC and United States rows of Zillow's metro ZHVI files (condo, sfr, sfrcondo; mid tier, smoothed, seasonally adjusted) | curl files.zillowstatic.com |
+| `raw/acs2024-B25002-*.json`, `raw/acs2024-B25004-*.json` | ACS 2020-2024 5-year occupancy and vacancy status, Horry County and Myrtle Beach city | curl data.census.gov/api/access |
+| `raw/t12c043.txt`, `raw/t27c031.txt` | S.C. Code Title 12 Chapter 43 and Title 27 Chapter 31 (Horizontal Property Act), scstatehouse.gov | curl |
+| `raw/tax-levy-2026.txt` | Horry County Auditor, 2026 tax levies, certified 7/27/2026 | curl, pdftotext |
+| `raw/fnma-b4-2.1-03.txt` | Fannie Mae Selling Guide B4-2.1-03, Ineligible Projects (08/05/2026), guide published October 7, 2026 | curl |
+| `raw/google-suggestions.txt` | Google search suggestions for 43 seed queries | `sh pull-suggestions.sh` |
+
+Inputs from other folders: Horry County deeds recorded 2025-10-01 to 2026-09-30, `data/2026-10-d/sell-out-of-state-buyers/out-of-state-buyers.json` (13,194 kept home sales; ships in Blog-Brain `batches/2026-10-d/sell-out-of-state-buyers/web.patch`).
+
+Kept out of the repo (PINs, per-parcel owner states, size), in the scratch RAW folder: `condo-parcels.json` (every condo unit parcel, layer 24: PIN, legal description, tax district, land use, values, owner mailing state, sale date; no owner name or street), `flood-points.json` (layer 19 zones at each sale point), `condo-sales-subset.json`.
+
+Definitions:
+- **Condo unit:** a residential parcel (land use 1xx) with a building value whose county legal description contains "HPR" (horizontal property regime, a condo under S.C. Code Title 27 Chapter 31).
+- **Main home:** the parcel's assessed value is under 5 percent of its taxable value, which is the 4 percent legal-residence ratio.
+- **Area:** county tax district 550 is North Myrtle Beach; 88x and 89x are the City of Myrtle Beach; 660 Surfside Beach; 110 Conway; the rest is outside city limits or in other towns. The codes were matched to places by joining the deed file's Census place to each sold parcel's tax district.
+- **Flood zone:** the FEMA zone at the sold parcel's center point. Layer 19 maps only VE, AE, A and the shaded 0.2 percent zone; a point with no polygon is outside the mapped flood areas (zone X).
diff --git a/data/2026-11-a/invest-condos/analyze.py b/data/2026-11-a/invest-condos/analyze.py
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..bff6437c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/data/2026-11-a/invest-condos/analyze.py
@@ -0,0 +1,89 @@
+"""Findings for /invest/condos/ from public records. No PIN, address or owner name is written out.
+Inputs (scratch, kept out of the repo because they carry PINs):
+  RAW/condo-parcels.json   every condo unit parcel (fetch_condo_parcels.py)
+  RAW/flood-points.json    FEMA zone at each sale point (fetch_flood.py)
+  DEEDS                    batch 2026-10-d deed file out-of-state-buyers.json (Horry County deeds recorded 2025-10-01..2026-09-30)
+Run: RAW=<scratch> DEEDS=<file> python3 -I analyze.py <datadir>. Writes findings.json."""
+import json, os, sys, statistics as st, collections
+D = sys.argv[1]; RAW = os.environ["RAW"]
+P = json.load(open(os.path.join(RAW, "condo-parcels.json")))
+deeds = json.load(open(os.environ["DEEDS"]))["sales"]
+flood = json.load(open(os.path.join(RAW, "flood-points.json")))
+ratio = json.load(open(os.path.join(D, "raw", "ratio-counts.json")))
+def area(td):
+    td = str(td)
+    if td == "550": return "North Myrtle Beach"
+    if td[:2] in ("88", "89"): return "City of Myrtle Beach"
+    if td == "660": return "Surfside Beach"
+    if td in ("110",): return "Conway"
+    return "Outside city limits and other towns"
+def pct(a, b): return round(100 * a / b, 1) if b else None
+out = {"made": "analyze.py", "sources": {"parcels": P["query"] + " where " + P["where"] + " (read " + P["read"] + ")",
+       "deeds": "Horry County AcclaimWeb DEED (001), recorded 2025-10-01 to 2026-09-30, batch 2026-10-d pull and filters",
+       "flood": "Horry County GIS layer 19 'Flood Zones' (FEMA flood map), point query at each sale's parcel point"}}
+# 1. the stock
+rows = P["rows"]; n = len(rows)
+four = [r for r in rows if r["TaxableProp"] and r["AssessedProp"] < 0.05 * r["TaxableProp"]]
+oos = [r for r in rows if r["OwnerState"] and r["OwnerState"].strip() not in ("SC", "")]
+blds = collections.Counter(r["LegalDescr"].split(";")[0].strip() for r in rows)
+stock = {"units": n, "regimes_by_legal_name": len(blds), "units_4pct": len(four), "pct_4pct": pct(len(four), n),
+         "units_mailing_outside_sc": len(oos), "pct_mailing_outside_sc": pct(len(oos), n),
+         "median_county_market_value": st.median([r["MarketProp"] for r in rows if r["MarketProp"]]),
+         "other_homes": {"homes": ratio["counts"]["other_all"]["count"], "homes_4pct": ratio["counts"]["other_4pct"]["count"],
+                         "pct_4pct": pct(ratio["counts"]["other_4pct"]["count"], ratio["counts"]["other_all"]["count"])},
+         "by_area": {}}
+for a in sorted({area(r["TaxDistrict"]) for r in rows}):
+    g = [r for r in rows if area(r["TaxDistrict"]) == a]
+    stock["by_area"][a] = {"units": len(g), "pct_4pct": pct(sum(1 for r in g if r in four), len(g)),
+                           "pct_mailing_outside_sc": pct(sum(1 for r in g if r["OwnerState"] and r["OwnerState"].strip() not in ("SC", "")), len(g)),
+                           "median_county_market_value": st.median([r["MarketProp"] for r in g if r["MarketProp"]])}
+sizes = sorted(blds.values())
+stock["units_per_regime"] = {"median": st.median(sizes), "regimes_100_plus": sum(1 for s in sizes if s >= 100),
+                             "units_in_regimes_100_plus": sum(s for s in sizes if s >= 100)}
+out["stock"] = stock
+# 2. the sales
+cs = [x for x in deeds if x.get("condo")]; hs = [x for x in deeds if not x.get("condo")]
+def summ(g):
+    pr = [x["cons"] for x in g]
+    m = [x for x in g if x.get("owner_is_grantee") and x.get("where") in ("SC", "US", "CANADA", "OTHER")]
+    return {"sales": len(g), "median_price": st.median(pr), "quartiles": [round(q) for q in st.quantiles(pr, n=4)],
+            "builder_sales": sum(1 for x in g if x["builder"]), "matched_owner": len(m),
+            "pct_buyer_mailing_outside_sc": pct(sum(1 for x in m if x["where"] != "SC"), len(m)),
+            "under_200k": sum(1 for x in g if x["cons"] < 200000), "pct_under_200k": pct(sum(1 for x in g if x["cons"] < 200000), len(g))}
+out["sales"] = {"condo": summ(cs), "other": summ(hs)}
+PIN = {r["PIN"]: r for r in rows}
+by_area = collections.defaultdict(list)
+for x in cs:
+    r = PIN.get(int(x["pin"])) if str(x["pin"]).isdigit() else None
+    by_area[area(r["TaxDistrict"]) if r else "not in condo layer"].append(x)
+out["sales"]["condo_by_area"] = {a: {"sales": len(g), "median_price": st.median([x["cons"] for x in g])} for a, g in by_area.items()}
+grp = collections.Counter(x["legal"].split(";")[0].strip() for x in cs if x.get("legal"))
+top = []
+for name, k in grp.most_common(12):
+    g = [x for x in cs if x.get("legal", "").split(";")[0].strip() == name]
+    units = blds.get(name)
+    top.append({"legal_name": name, "sales": k, "units_in_regime": units, "pct_of_units_sold": pct(k, units) if units else None,
+                "median_price": st.median([x["cons"] for x in g]), "builder_sales": sum(1 for x in g if x["builder"])})
+out["sales"]["top_regimes_by_recorded_sales"] = top
+out["sales"]["regimes_with_a_sale"] = len(grp)
+# 3. flood zones at condo sale points
+def zone(x):
+    if not x.get("lat"): return None
+    v = flood.get(f"{x['lat']:.5f},{x['lon']:.5f}")
+    if v is None: return None
+    if not v: return "no zone mapped"
+    zs = {f["FLD_ZONE"] for f in v}
+    for z in ("VE", "AE", "A", "AO", "AH"):
+        if z in zs: return z
+    return "X" if "X" in zs else sorted(zs)[0]
+zc = collections.Counter(zone(x) for x in cs)
+known = sum(v for k, v in zc.items() if k)
+sfha = sum(v for k, v in zc.items() if k in ("VE", "AE", "A", "AO", "AH"))
+out["flood_condo_sales"] = {"sales_with_zone": known, "by_zone": {str(k): v for k, v in zc.most_common()},
+                            "pct_VE": pct(zc["VE"], known), "pct_AE": pct(zc["AE"], known), "pct_high_risk": pct(sfha, known)}
+zh = collections.Counter(zone(x) for x in hs)
+kh = sum(v for k, v in zh.items() if k)
+out["flood_other_sales"] = {"sales_with_zone": kh, "by_zone": {str(k): v for k, v in zh.most_common()},
+                            "pct_high_risk": pct(sum(v for k, v in zh.items() if k in ("VE", "AE", "A", "AO", "AH")), kh)}
+json.dump(out, open(os.path.join(D, "findings.json"), "w"), indent=1)
+print(json.dumps(out, indent=1))
diff --git a/data/2026-11-a/invest-condos/count_ratio.py b/data/2026-11-a/invest-condos/count_ratio.py
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..09c3734d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/data/2026-11-a/invest-condos/count_ratio.py
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+"""Counts of residential parcels with a building in Horry County GIS layer 24, condo units (legal description has 'HPR')
+against all other homes, and how many carry the 4 percent legal-residence ratio (AssessedProp under 5 percent of TaxableProp).
+Run: python3 -I count_ratio.py <datadir>. Writes raw/ratio-counts.json with every query URL."""
+import json, sys, time, urllib.request, urllib.parse
+D = sys.argv[1]; Q = "https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer/24/query?"
+BASE = "LandUseCode LIKE '1%' AND MarketImprv > 0"
+W = {"condo_all": BASE + " AND LegalDescr LIKE '%HPR%'", "condo_4pct": BASE + " AND LegalDescr LIKE '%HPR%' AND AssessedProp < TaxableProp*0.05",
+     "other_all": BASE + " AND LegalDescr NOT LIKE '%HPR%'", "other_4pct": BASE + " AND LegalDescr NOT LIKE '%HPR%' AND AssessedProp < TaxableProp*0.05"}
+out = {"read": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d"), "layer": Q[:-7], "counts": {}}
+for k, w in W.items():
+    url = Q + urllib.parse.urlencode({"where": w, "returnCountOnly": "true", "f": "json"})
+    n = json.load(urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=120))["count"]
+    out["counts"][k] = {"where": w, "url": url, "count": n}; print(k, n)
+json.dump(out, open(D + "/raw/ratio-counts.json", "w"), indent=1)
diff --git a/data/2026-11-a/invest-condos/fetch_condo_parcels.py b/data/2026-11-a/invest-condos/fetch_condo_parcels.py
